   "l": "the female, abidingly, by stillness overcomes the male;\nby stillness she makes herself low.",
   "v": true,
   "i": "The female always overcomes the male through stillness; through stillness she takes the lower place.",
   "n": "為下 is 'to act as the lower', 為 being the ordinary verb 'to do, to make, to serve as' — the house reading is wéi unless the character governs a noun in the sense 'for the sake of', which it does not here.\n\nWang Bi's comment is one line: still, and not seeking, and things come to it of themselves. The argument is not that softness is virtuous but that the lower position is where things arrive."
